# Chrome extension build configuration.
#
# The build (build.mjs) has safe built-in defaults for both modes; create
# .env.development.local / .env.production.local (both covered by the repo's
# .env.*.local gitignore rule — use these exact names) only to override them.
# Never commit real environment values; development Clerk-instance identifiers
# in particular must stay out of the public repo.
#
# Values are strictly validated: KEY=VALUE lines only (no quotes), no unknown
# or duplicate keys, and URLs must be bare origins (scheme + host + port; a
# lone trailing slash is normalized away).
#
# Current variables (all optional):
#   TIDDLY_API_URL   Backend API origin. Defaults: development
#                    http://localhost:8000, production https://api.tiddly.me.
#                    Also drives the generated manifest's host_permissions.
#                    Pinned in production (a differing override fails the
#                    build — add a distinct build mode instead); development
#                    allows http for loopback hosts only.
#
# The Clerk session-sync milestone adds required variables here (publishable
# key, sync host, Frontend API origin) — the development values for those have
# no defaults and must come from your .env.development.local.
